<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates fall in all maturities.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates fall in all maturities.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) fell across the board on Wednesday in reaction to the slide in Treasury bill rates, traders said.</p>
<p>Banks also saw dollar inflows for placement in fixed income securities in advance of any further falls in interest rates.</p>
<p>The inflows are adding to the liquidity in the system, dealers added.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  MAY 14		 MAY 13</p>
<p>    1 W		9 15/16		 10  1/8</p>
<p>    2 W		9 15/16		 10  1/16</p>
<p>    1 M		9 13/16		 9 15/16</p>
<p>    2 M		9  7/8		  10  1/16</p>
<p>    3 M		9 15/16		 10  1/8</p>
<p>    6 M		10  1/4		 10  3/8</p>
<p>    12M		10  9/16		10 11/16</p>
<p>    VAL		15-May		  14-May</p>
<p>-- LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (63 2) 841-8937</p>
</text>
